+# Remaining underlying records
+
+These supplement existing SPT01–SPT08/SR01 and FAA01–FAA04; they do not create replacement master IDs or narrow the original scope. No request was sent.
+
+- **Port Authority letter chain:** original January 24 letter, routing corresponding to the apparent January 28 stamp, NIST's actual confirmation, rejection or qualification, attachments and subsequent correspondence. A reply could establish what was accepted or disputed; a request alone cannot.
+- **Authority for the testimony language:** contemporaneous existing rules, advice and decision records identifying covered persons and scope. The single inspected statutory paragraph is not a survey of every possible authority. Preserve contrary explanations and any nonacceptance.
+- **Earlier instruments:** the actual Port Authority agreement described in the March hearing and the separate FEMA confidentiality instrument, signatures/versions and drawing-release receipts. Do not assume the NIST support letter is that earlier agreement.
+- **Cooperation and performance:** January 10 briefing package, invitations/attendance/notes, originals of the agency support letters, actual delivery/access records and proposed independent-panel appointment, charge and review materials. A statement of intent is not completed performance.
+- **Unverified text-layer dates:** the ASCE first-page text in B161 reads November 15, 2001; continuation headers read September 15, 2001. Both strings are preserved. Those page images were not inspected here, so no historical date contradiction, preferred value or cause is asserted. Verify the images before using this as an anomaly.
+- **Unfinished physical chains:** yard/workbook/marking/coupon/transfer originals, W14A/W14B building-attribution rationale, C12a/b and FEMA Sample1 joins, and native contractor drafts/comments/delivery remain open.
+- **Audio:** direct or independently checked listening; source-channel meaning; original cassette/native rerecording, certification, custody and independent clock anchors. The recovered control lacks its internal process exit receipt. Further desired-word tuning is not an accepted substitute.
+- **Full goal:** actual FAA correction/delivery and signed disposition; carrier/operator and source-to-exhibit joins; recorder/configuration/clock inputs; native materials measurements/custody; and steel preservation/attribution decisions remain required in their existing work queues.
+
+A native response could weaken or strengthen concerns. No missing item is classified as never created, withheld, destroyed or evidence of motive merely because this review has not acquired it.
